{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfS5f5yP5miNgnGM2p8pL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Conventions this repository already has:**\n- Error handling uses sealed `ApiException` with typed subclasses (`ConflictException` for 409, `ResourceNotFoundException` for 404)\n- ErrorCode enum contains the closed set of error codes (line 31-37 in ApiError.kt)\n- GlobalExceptionHandler (line 16-28) converts all ApiExceptions to standard error envelopes\n- Controllers return `ResponseEntity` with explicit status (line 43 in ShipmentController.kt), or just data (Spring wraps it)\n- Tests use `MockMvc` with `@SpringBootTest` and `@AutoConfigureMockMvc`\n- In-memory repository uses `ConcurrentHashMap` and `save()` method persists by key replacement\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. **ApiError.kt** — must add error code for CANCELLED shipments (409 conflict)\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — must add `confirm` endpoint; cannot avoid without losing functionality\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — must add tests for confirm behavior (4 cases per requirement)\n\n**Risks:**\n- ErrorCode enum is closed/public API — adding a code changes the contract but is necessary\n- Idempotent logic: if already `CONFIRMED`, must return success without state change (not persist identical object again)\n- Persisting the modified shipment: `repository.save()` must be called or change is lost\n\n**Open questions:**\n- What error code name to use for CANCELLED? Repository does not define one. The requirement says \"consistent with the rest of this API\" — looking at existing codes (`SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS`, `ORDER_NOT_FOUND`), I'll use `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` to indicate the shipment exists but is in a state that cannot be confirmed.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt**: Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` to the `ErrorCode` enum. This code signals a shipment exists but is in a terminal state that cannot be confirmed (e.g., already `CANCELLED`). It will be paired with HTTP 409 via `ConflictException`.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add a new `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` method with signature `fun confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String): ResponseEntity<Shipment>`. The method will:\n   - Fetch the shipment via `repository.findById(shipmentId)`, throwing `ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND)` if null (404 case)\n   - Check the shipment's current status:\n     - If `CANCELLED`, throw `ConflictException(SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS, ...)` (409 case)\n     - If `CREATED`, update it to `CONFIRMED` via `repository.save()` and return it\n     - If `CONFIRMED`, return it unchanged (idempotent; no save needed)\n   - Return `ResponseEntity.ok(shipment)` with HTTP 200\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add four tests:\n   - `confirms a CREATED shipment and returns CONFIRMED` — create, confirm, verify status changed to CONFIRMED\n   - `confirm of already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds without change` — create, confirm twice, verify second call returns 200 and status still CONFIRMED\n   - `confirm of CANCELLED shipment is rejected with 409` — set up CANCELLED shipment directly in repository, confirm it, verify 409 and error code is SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS\n   - `confirm of non-existent shipment is rejected with 404` — confirm non-existent ID, verify 404 and error code is SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- **Use PUT instead of POST**: The requirement explicitly names `POST`. While idempotency is more semantically associated with PUT, this API uses POST for create, so confirming (a state transition) also uses POST.\n- **Create a separate service layer**: The existing codebase has no service layer; the controller directly calls the repository. Adding one would be architectural refactoring outside the scope.\n- **Use update/merge pattern in repository**: The repository already implements save-by-key-replacement via `ConcurrentHashMap[key] = value`. No new repository method is needed.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Response | Mechanism |\n|------|------|-------|----------|-----------|\n| CREATED → CONFIRMED | findById(id) | save(modified copy) | Shipment + 200 OK | ResponseEntity.ok() |\n| Already CONFIRMED (retry) | findById(id) | _(nothing)_ | Shipment + 200 OK | ResponseEntity.ok() (no save) |\n| CANCELLED | findById(id) | _(nothing)_ | Error + 409 | throw ConflictException → GlobalExceptionHandler |\n| Not found | findById(id) returns null | _(nothing)_ | Error + 404 | throw ResourceNotFoundException → GlobalExceptionHandler |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **Test**: `confirms a CREATED shipment` — POST /shipments with create request, verify CREATED status, POST /shipments/{id}/confirm, verify status is CONFIRMED in response\n2. **Test**: `confirm retry succeeds` — Create, confirm once, confirm again, verify second call returns 200 with CONFIRMED status (no exception)\n3. **Test**: `confirm CANCELLED is rejected` — Create, manually set status to CANCELLED in repository, POST /shipments/{id}/confirm, verify 409 with error code SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS\n4. **Test**: `confirm non-existent is rejected` — POST /shipments/unknown-id/confirm, verify 404 with error code SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\n**Step 1: Add the error code**"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1895,"cache_read_input_tokens":15732,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1895},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0ba624ae-7a91-44bb-baf1-b58683d2d290","uuid":"6cdd7e6c-b52a-4a86-95ff-8f3fa6bd2ddc","timestamp":"2026-09-26T12:51:38.608Z","request_id":"req_011CfS5f5c4HinRkH9zZHk